  "period_end": "2025-10-31",
  "title": "The API became easier to actually use",
  "summary": "October made Pollinations easier to reach from real apps, broadened its model and image tooling, and gave Hacktoberfest contributors more places to plant things.\n\nRewritten docs, Bearer tokens, browser CORS, simpler GET text generation, and copyable frontend keys reduced the distance between an idea and a working HTTP call.\n\nGPT-5-mini, Claude 4.5 Haiku, Azure Flux Kontext, Azure OpenAI Nano 5, and nanobanana expanded the lineup while clearer refusals, image sizing, queue tuning, and safety timeouts made generation more legible and reliable.\n\nNew project ideas, contributor guidance, automated subdomain deployments, and tools like the opposite-prompt generator gave community work a clearer path from issue to something people can visit.\n\nThe Creative Projects directory added a steady run of community apps, from virtual makeup and AI dungeon masters to image transformation and dream decoding. An HTTP endpoint remains a remarkably effective seed packet.",
